+# 🌉 Bridge Work Order — [P2] Core package hygiene: 16 KB god-init with triple-fallback imports, dead exports, _archive/ committed in active repo (bridge-20261027-core-hygiene)
+
+## Problem
+Verified by direct code read + tree scan 2026-10-25:
+
+1. `core/__init__.py` is **16 KB**: three-level `try/except ImportError` chains (relative → bare → absolute), a QA-suite import guard added as an incident-#9 patch, a PEP 562 lazy loader bolted on, and **permanently-`None` dead exports still advertised in `__all__`** (`DigitalTwinWorldModel = None`, `TheoryOfMindSystem = None`, `ToMConfig = None`, …)
+2. Umbrella repo tree: **5,372 files**, including `_archive/batch-1/` + `_archive/batch-2/` committed inside the active repo (old backend code: firestore_helpers, shared_workspace, brand_compliance) — while a dedicated `Supremeai-bd/supremeai-archive` repo already exists
+3. Consequences already paid: pytest collection 30 s+, `import scout` ≈ 11 s (documented in the file's own comments), AI builders waste work orders on archive files, PR Guardian diff-metrics get noise
+
+## Impact (AIQ mapping)
+- AIQ-036 ❌ maintainable code (verified)
+- AIQ-109 🟡 traceability: `__all__` lies about what exists
+- AIQ-104 🟡 test noise + collection time
+
+## Fix (smallest safe change)
+1. Flatten import chains to one canonical package-relative path per symbol; keep lazy loader ONLY for torch-dependent research exports
+2. Remove permanently-None symbols from `__all__`; add a unit test asserting every `__all__` entry is importable-and-not-None
+3. `git mv` `_archive/` content to the `supremeai-archive` repo (preserve history via `git filter-repo` or subtree push); add `_archive/` to `.gitignore`
+4. Extract `get_complete_ai_system`/`run_complete_system_test` into `core/selfcheck.py`
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+- [ ] Importing `core` in a fresh interpreter exposes `core.EWC` successfully; no triple-fallback blocks remain
+- [ ] `__all__` contains zero permanently-None symbols (test enforced)
+- [ ] Umbrella tree < 3,000 files; no `_archive` paths on main
+- [ ] `import core` cold time reduced (before/after numbers in evidence)
+
+## Reflection Evidence (why + alternatives_rejected)
+**Why:** every future builder agent pays the import tax and the misleading `__all__` on every task.
+**Alternatives rejected:** (a) deleting dead symbols outright — breaks external import contracts silently; the lazy-None contract is kept where torch deps genuinely decide availability.
+
+## Labels
+`bridge:queued` `P2-medium` `area:core` `tech-debt` `AIQ:036` `AIQ:109`
